gpuServingVllm: accept extra engine arguments

THE GAP. The template renders a closed list of five engine arguments with no way to add one. A request carrying `tools`
is rejected outright unless the engine was started with --enable-auto-tool-choice and a --tool-call-parser, and every
request a coding agent sends carries tools. So a chart that serves an OpenAI-compatible endpoint cannot serve what an
OpenAI-compatible coding agent actually sends.

OBSERVED: HTTP 400, `"auto" tool choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and --tool-call-parser to be set`, on every
request, with no way to fix it through the chart.

THE FIX appends a caller-supplied list after the rendered arguments. Default is an empty list, so the rendered
Deployment is byte-identical for anyone not setting it (checked by rendering both ways). The parser name is
model-specific, so the chart deliberately holds no table of them.

The same closed-list shape is in neuron-serving-vllm.yaml, which additionally fixes --max-num-seqs and --max-model-len
by value; left alone here to keep this patch to one template.

Sent as a request to the project separately. Delete this patch once it is upstream -- tierbook-up detects that itself.
---
diff --git a/infra/eks/charts/experiments/templates/gpu-serving-vllm.yaml b/infra/eks/charts/experiments/templates/gpu-serving-vllm.yaml
index 9d23da7..2135797 100644
--- a/infra/eks/charts/experiments/templates/gpu-serving-vllm.yaml
+++ b/infra/eks/charts/experiments/templates/gpu-serving-vllm.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,9 @@ spec:
             - --max-model-len={{ $v.maxModelLen | default 4096 }}
             - --gpu-memory-utilization={{ $v.gpuMemoryUtilization | default "0.85" }}
             - --port={{ $v.port | default 8000 }}
+            {{- range $v.extraArgs | default list }}
+            - {{ . | quote }}
+            {{- end }}
           env:
             # HF token for gated models (optional; ungated models need no token).
             - name: HF_TOKEN
diff --git a/infra/eks/charts/experiments/values.yaml b/infra/eks/charts/experiments/values.yaml
index 9becd67..f106371 100644
--- a/infra/eks/charts/experiments/values.yaml
+++ b/infra/eks/charts/experiments/values.yaml
@@ -443,6 +443,16 @@ gpuServingVllm:
   maxModelLen: 4096
   gpuMemoryUtilization: "0.85"
   port: 8000
+  # Extra engine flags, appended verbatim to the args above. Empty by default, so the rendered Deployment is unchanged
+  # for anyone not setting it.
+  #
+  # The case this exists for: a request carrying `tools` is rejected outright unless the engine was started with
+  # `--enable-auto-tool-choice` and a `--tool-call-parser`, and every request a coding agent sends carries tools. The
+  # parser name is model-specific (hermes, llama3_json, mistral, ...), so this chart deliberately does not hold a table
+  # of them -- a table here is a table that goes stale.
+  #
+  #   extraArgs: ["--enable-auto-tool-choice", "--tool-call-parser=hermes"]
+  extraArgs: []
   readinessInitialDelaySeconds: 60
   readinessPeriodSeconds: 10
   readinessFailureThreshold: 90
